# The bff image's build context is this repo's root. Without this file the
# whole tree — including a ~1400-package node_modules and the git history —
# is uploaded to the daemon on every build.
#
# Note the image installs dependencies itself from package.json + bun.lock
# (see docker/bff.Dockerfile), so excluding node_modules is required for
# correctness as well as speed: a host node_modules built for a different
# platform must never be copied in.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
web/dist/
# Git: metadata only. The bff image's buildinfo stage reads HEAD and the refs to
# stamp the build with its commit (docker/bff.Dockerfile), which needs the refs
# and absolutely none of the objects — the history is not a build input and does
# not belong in an image layer or an uploaded context. That covers a build made
# from a real checkout; a deploy manager's copy of the tree has no `.git` at all,
# and its build is deliberately unstamped (`+unknown`).
.git/**
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs/**
!.git/packed-refs
.ui-check/
# Worktrees are build context twice over otherwise — `.dev-flow/<slug>/worktree` is where dev-flow puts
# them now. `.worktrees/` stays listed for a machine still holding checkouts from before the move: it
# is no longer created, but if one is left on disk the build context (the repo root) drags it in.
.dev-flow/
.worktrees/
*.log

# Secrets and local state — none of it belongs in an image layer.
docker/secrets/
docker/.env
.env
.env.local
